-- title:
--   The place j=a has residue field K
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $a \in K$. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC K 1` for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the two series `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K 1`, and let $v =$ `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint K a` be the place of $F$ over $K$ obtained by transporting, along the isomorphism `ratFuncEquivCharLOneC K` of $K(T)$ with $F$ (which fixes $K$ pointwise), the finite place of the rational function field $K(T)$ attached to the irreducible polynomial $T - a$. Here a place of $F$ over $K$ consists of a valuation subring of $F$ which contains the image of $K$, is not the whole of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring, and its residue field is the residue field of that local ring. The assertion is that the structure map $K \to \kappa(v)$, i.e. `algebraMap` into the residue field of $v$, is surjective; since it is a field homomorphism, $\kappa(v) = K$.
--
--   This is the rationality (residue degree one) statement for the points $j = a$ of the $j$-line: the closed point of $\mathbb{A}^1_K$ cut out by $T - a$ is $K$-rational. It is what gives a function regular at such a place a well-defined value in $K$, and it is used in the treatment of the nodal specialisation of the modular curve, for instance by [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_and_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_pole_not_centred`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_and_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_pole_not_centred) and [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.eval2_branch_eq_zero_of_modularEval_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.eval2_branch_eq_zero_of_modularEval_eq_zero).
